# DTF tier manifest: conda-virtual-shards  (artifact-keeper#4607 / #4612 / #4608)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=mock-conda-sharded (the CEP-16
# upstream channels of harness/tiers/conda-sharded-remote-virtual/fixtures)
# + limits.conda-merge-gate (passes the merge gate's env knobs through)
# + logging.json-file (the #4612 case greps the backend's warn line).
#
# THE BUGS (all fixed in 1.11.0, on top of #4577's remote/virtual shards)
# #4607  a virtual listed an upstream shard that holds only a `removed` entry
#        (conda-forge's 90-byte cuda-nvcc_linux-64 noarch shard) and then
#        answered 404 for it, which pixi/rattler treat as fatal.
# #4612  an upstream shard index past the 8 MiB metadata tier answered 502 on
#        the remote (conda-pypi's noarch index is 28.6 MB); now read again
#        under a 64 MiB ceiling, and an index past THAT is 404 ("publishes no
#        CEP-16 shard index ... use repodata.json") on the remote and on a
#        virtual over it, never 502.
# #4608  every virtual merge request ran its own merge (20 concurrent solves
#        took the backend to 20.8 GB); now one shared merge kept under one
#        ETag, a cap on concurrent merges and a 503 + Retry-After queue
#        deadline, with ak_conda_virtual_merge_* metrics.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   GET /conda/{virtual}/noarch/repodata_shards.msgpack.zst + every shard
#   GET /conda/{remote|virtual}/noarch/repodata_shards.msgpack.zst over a
#       9.7 MiB and a 70.4 MiB upstream index
#   20 x GET /conda/{virtual}/noarch/repodata.json in parallel, If-None-Match
#   GET /api/v1/admin/metrics (ak_conda_virtual_merge_*)
#   a merge held 9 s by a slow upstream while a second virtual's merge queues
#
# Merge gate: ONE merge slot and a 2 s queue deadline, so the second merge is
# shed with 503 while the slow one runs. Every other case is sequential (one
# merge at a time), so the cap does not change their outcome.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~60 calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the remotes' upstream is the mock on a
# private address.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-conda-sharded limits.conda-merge-gate logging.json-file"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
export CONDA_VIRTUAL_MAX_CONCURRENT_MERGES="1"
export CONDA_VIRTUAL_MERGE_QUEUE_SECS="2"
